# Important Interview Points

✅ Structured Output returns data in a predefined format.

✅ It is mainly used for databases, APIs, and AI agents.

✅ `with_structured_output()` tells the model to follow a schema.

✅ Pydantic is the recommended approach for production Python applications.

✅ TypedDict is simpler but provides fewer features.

✅ JSON Schema is useful when multiple programming languages are involved.

---

# Summary

Structured Output is a technique that makes Large Language Models return responses in a fixed, organized format instead of plain text.

It allows AI applications to easily integrate with databases, APIs, and other software systems while producing reliable and consistent outputs.

